   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Mike!</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for the quick response! <br></div><div><br></div><div>It seems like I at least figured out a work around for the issue. After uninstalling and reinstalling all my r files and packages and still getting the same error, I did some digging and found this <a href=\"https://github.com/Unidata/netcdf-c/issues/1299\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/Unidata/netcdf-c/issues/1299&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793240153533000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0U51NzxouzoQ0JW73Iz0vw\">https://github.com/Unidata/netcdf-c/issues/1299</a>. With all my libraries and packages up to date, the below code still wont work:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>nc &lt;- RNetCDF::<a href=\"http://open.nc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://open.nc&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793240153533000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0bbi7PedSp-APXWNc0MOJJ\">open.nc</a>(paste0(baseurl, &quot;tmmn_1979_CurrentYear_CONUS.nc&quot;))</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>However, this code works just fine:</div><div><br></div><div>nc &lt;- RNetCDF::<a href=\"http://open.nc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://open.nc&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793240153533000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0bbi7PedSp-APXWNc0MOJJ\">open.nc</a>(paste0(baseurl, &quot;tmmn_1979_CurrentYear_CONUS.nc#fillmismatch&quot;))</div><div><br></div><div>Given that, I went into my version of micro_usa()  and suffixed that \r\n#fillmismatch\r\n\r\nonto any instance of it calling data from the 1979_CurrentYear_CONUS database. Everything&#39;s back up and working for me now!</div><div>Unsure if this is a consistent issue with the most updated versions of \r\nRNetCDF, something from the data provider, or if my computer is just having its own issues, but maybe this will be helpful somewhere down the line!</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Connor<br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, Sep 17, 2021 at 10:52 PM NicheMapR &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nich...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
